---
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import journalCover2026 from "../../assets/ESS-journal-2026.jpg";
---

<Layout title="ESS Journal of Theology, Humanities, Arts and Sciences - Maiden Edition. | ECWA Society for Scholars">
  <Header />
  <div class="plus-jakarta-sans-normal">
    <div class="bg-[#faf5ee] py-10">
      <div class="w-full max-w-full px-4 sm:px-6 md:px-8 lg:max-w-5xl xl:max-w-6xl 2xl:max-w-7xl mx-auto">
        <div class="text-xs space-x-2">
          <a href="/" class="text-[#06005A] hover:opacity-60">
            Home
          </a>
          <span>/</span>
          <a href="/news-and-events" class="text-[#06005A] hover:opacity-60">
            News & Events
          </a>
          <span>/</span>
          <span class="text-black">Read</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="font-bold text-3xl mt-2 libre-baskerville-bold uppercase">
          ESS Journal of Theology, Humanities, Arts and Sciences - Maiden
          Edition.
        </h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="py-20">
      <div class="w-full max-w-full px-4 sm:px-6 md:px-8 lg:max-w-5xl xl:max-w-6xl 2xl:max-w-7xl mx-auto">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-20">
          <div>
            <div class="w-full bg-cyan-800 h-0.5"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="news col-span-2 space-y-6 text-base text-slate-600">
            <p>
              <Image
                src={journalCover2026}
                alt="Cover pages of the ESS Journal - Maiden Edition"
                class="h-full w-full object-cover object-center transition-transform duration-300 ease-in-out group-hover:scale-110 group-hover:grayscale-0"
              />
            </p>
            <p>
              The ESS Journal of Theology, Humanities, Arts and Sciences is an
              academic publication of the ECWA Society for Scholars (ESS),
              established to provide a platform for scholarly research,
              intellectual engagement and the dissemination of knowledge across
              theology, humanities, arts and sciences.
            </p>
            <p>
              The maiden edition brings together scholarly contributions
              addressing important theological, social, ethical, educational and
              developmental issues. Through interdisciplinary perspectives, the
              journal explores the relationship between Christian faith,
              academic scholarship and contemporary societal challenges.
            </p>
            <p>
              This edition features thought-provoking research on faith and
              science, Christian theology, civic rights, human dignity,
              religious education, sustainable development, jurisprudence and
              social transformation.
            </p>
            <p>The maiden edition features the following scholarly articles:</p>
            <ol class="list-decimal mx-10 space-y-4">
              <li>
                <b>Bridging the Gap between Faith and Science in the Church</b>
                <br />
                <i>Ngutor Isaac Anga</i> - Page 1
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>
                  Christians and the Civic Right to Protest: A Pastoral
                  Theological Examination of Civic Protest and Its Implication
                  to the Nigerian Church
                </b>
                <br />
                <i>Yakubu Yusuf Jakhengo</i> - Page 20
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>
                  Faith in Genesis 45:1–5 and the Art of Forgiveness in
                  Christian Theology: A Reflection on Healing and Reconciliation
                  for Church Service to Humanity
                </b>
                <br />
                <i>Bulus Audu Makama, PhD</i> - Page 46
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>
                  God of Last-Minute Interventions: A Theological and Narrative
                  Analysis of Divine Responses to Human Prayers in the New
                  Testament
                </b>
                <br />
                <i>Azariah G. Akawu</i> - Page 60
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>
                  Poverty Eradication as a Moral Imperative in Restoring Human
                  Dignity
                </b>
                <br />
                <i>Joel Hassan Nyam, PhD</i> - Page 71
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>
                  Religious Education for National Cohesion and Transformation
                </b>
                <br />
                <i>Ngutor Isaac Anga</i> - Page 88
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>
                  Religious Scholarship, Human Dignity, and Sustainable
                  Development: The Africa Evangelical Theological Perspective
                </b>
                <br />
                <i>Phinehas Tom Kadam</i> - Page 105
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>
                  Deuteronomic Jurisprudence and National Development: The
                  Ethics of Righteous Decisions
                </b>
                <br />
                <i>Dr. Solomon Amao</i> - Page 122
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>
                  Pastorate Lapses Obstructing Human Dignity and Development
                  Among the Evangelicals in Contemporary Nigeria
                </b>
                <br />
                <i>David Gbenga S. Atteh</i> - Page 140
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>
                  Empowerment and Spiritual Action for Freedom: A Blueprint for
                  Personal Transformation and Social Liberation
                </b>
                <br />
                <i>Christiana BEST, PhD</i> - Page 150
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>
                  Theological and Methodological Frameworks for Sustainable Food
                  Security: Integrating Biblical Mandates, Agricultural
                  Stewardship, and Social Protection in Developing Nations
                </b>
                <br />
                <i>Ezra Bako Amans, PhD</i> - Page 163
              </li>
            </ol>

            <p>
              Get your copy of the maiden edition of the ESS Journal of
              Theology, Humanities, Arts and Sciences and explore its collection
              of scholarly articles.
            </p>
            <p>
              To order a copy, kindly make payment to the following bank
              account:
            </p>
            <ul class="list-disc mx-10 space-y-4">
              <li>
                <b>Bank:</b> Gowans Microfinance Bank
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>Account Type:</b> Savings
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>Account Number:</b> 1100187704
              </li>
              <li>
                <b>Account Name:</b> ECWA Scholars Conference
              </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
              After making payment: Kindly retain your payment receipt as proof
              of payment and contact the ECWA Society for Scholars for further
              information on obtaining your copy:
              <a
                href="http://wa.me/2348066259948"
                target="_blank"
                class="text-[#06005A] hover:opacity-60"
              >
                Contact Secretariat Secretary
              </a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!--  -->
  </div>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
